            ],
            "Pi"
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Cut the region into thin sectors by rays from the pole. A sector of radius r and small angle \\( \\Delta\\theta \\) has area \\( \\frac{1}{2} r^{2} \\Delta\\theta \\), the fraction \\( \\frac{\\Delta\\theta}{2\\pi} \\) of the disc of area \\( \\pi r^{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "area of a circular sector"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Adding the sectors and letting the angles shrink turns the sum into an integral over the angles the region sweeps, so the area is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\int_{0}^{\\pi} \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 13\\right)^{2}\\,d\\theta \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99048",
         "rule_named": "polar area integral"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating the integral gives \\( 78 + \\frac{347 \\pi}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            78,
